{
  "title": "Valid Sudoku",
  "description": "A Sudoku board is given as a list of 9 strings, one per row from top to bottom. Each string has 9 characters: a digit `1` to `9`, or `.` for an empty cell.\n\nThe board is **valid** when no digit appears twice in any row, in any column, or in any of the nine 3 by 3 boxes. Empty cells are ignored, and the board does not need to be solvable.\n\nReturn `true` if the board is valid and `false` otherwise.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- `board.size() == 9` and every row has exactly 9 characters.\n- Every character is a digit `1` to `9` or `.`.\n- Inputs are passed as function arguments and the answer is returned from the function. Do not read from standard input or print the result.\n",
  "reference": "bool is_valid_sudoku(vector<string> board) {\n    bool rows[9][9] = {}, cols[9][9] = {}, boxes[9][9] = {};\n    for (int r = 0; r < 9; ++r) {\n        for (int c = 0; c < 9; ++c) {\n            if (board[r][c] == '.') {\n                continue;\n            }\n            int d = board[r][c] - '1';\n            int b = (r / 3) * 3 + c / 3;\n            if (rows[r][d] || cols[c][d] || boxes[b][d]) {\n                return false;\n            }\n            rows[r][d] = cols[c][d] = boxes[b][d] = true;\n        }\n    }\n    return true;\n}\n",
  "template": "bool is_valid_sudoku(vector<string> board) {\n    // Return whether no row, column, or box repeats a digit.\n    return false;\n}\n",
  "tags": [
    "Arrays",
    "Hash Tables",
    "Matrix"
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "test_number": 0,
      "explanation": "No row, column, or 3 by 3 box contains the same digit twice, so the board is valid. It does not matter that many cells are still empty."
    },
    {
      "test_number": 1,
      "explanation": "The top-left cell is now 8, but the first column already has an 8 in the fourth row, and so does the top-left box. A repeated digit makes the board invalid."
    }
  ],
